The attached image illustrates the in vivo kinetics of Alexa Fluor 647-labeled Nano-11 nanoparticles following intramuscular injection, demonstrating their retention and clearance. Panel (a) shows whole-mouse fluorescence imaging, revealing that Nano-11 is primarily retained at the injection site and gradually diminishes over 21 days. Panel (b) confirms the absence of Nano-11 accumulation in internal organs by day 21, indicating a lack of systemic distribution. Panel (c) quantifies the fluorescence intensity at the injection site over time, showing a decrease that signifies gradual clearance, which supports Nano-11's potential as a safe and effective vaccine adjuvant without long-term deposition in tissues.